+/* NewDarkVR (port/core/vr_stereo.c): the held weapon. After its scene render the engine clears the depth buffer only
+ * (flags = D3DCLEAR_ZBUFFER) and draws the first-person weapon with screen-space vertices, using the camera of the last
+ * scene render. It places the weapon relative to its own camera (which follows the gun hand). So, per frame:
+ *   1. vr_d3d_gun_pass(1): after the eye renders, one more scene render from the engine's own camera, of which nothing
+ *      is drawn and no clear done; it only leaves the engine's camera in place for the weapon;
+ *   2. vr_d3d_gun_pass(3) until EndScene: the weapon's draws (which the engine batches and sends at EndScene) are kept, not drawn (vertex data, indices and state), and
+ *      their camera-space bounding box measured (x right, y down, z forward, engine units: z = 1 / rhw,
+ *      x = (sx - cx) z / f);
+ *   3. vr_d3d_gun_replay_eye, at the end of the frame: per eye, the kept draws are moved by a 3x4 matrix (engine camera
+ *      space to eye camera space: the hand), projected for the eye and drawn into the eye's image after a depth clear. */
